      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DON'T DOUBT DARCY (1) is the one to beat off a single debut run that had more merit than the bare fourth suggests, having raced keenly and wide before being beaten just over three lengths as a well-supported favourite at Kembla Grange. The easy Warwick Farm trial win gives him a sound platform to return from a long break, and the exposed form in this line-up is not deep. HIT THE RUNWAY (6) is the key debutante, drawn to get every chance and coming through a solid Warwick Farm trial for a stable with strong first-starter output. Tongue-tie goes on and no shock to see her get the better of these. WILD COURAGE (10) has been competitive in small fields and was only beaten a length and a half first-up at Newcastle. Ready to aim up from the rails gate. REGAL PROFIT (5) Capitalist colt from Still Reigning on debut for the Portelli yard. Impressed in both trial wins and looks to have the ability to overcome the sticky gate.",
